description:
We are seeking a thoughtful and highly collaborative UX Designer to help shape exceptional user experiences across a suite of product platforms. In this role, you will take ownership of day-to-day UX project work, driving design execution from concept through delivery while ensuring consistency, usability, and alignment with business goals. You will partner closely with product managers, engineers, and stakeholders to translate user needs and insights into intuitive, engaging experiences that elevate our products and deliver real value to users.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
This is a hybrid role based out of Sun Prairie, WI.
&nbsp;
&nbsp;

- Collaborate with engineering, product management, and research teams to ensure system adoption and technical feasibility.&nbsp;

- Balance consistency and flexibility to support diverse product needs while maintaining brand alignment.&nbsp;

- Drive cross-platform consistency across mobile applications, embedded systems, and related digital experiences.&nbsp;

- Advocate for user-centered design practices and measurable UX outcomes.&nbsp;

- Monitor usage of metrics and feedback to continuously improve the system and its adoption.&nbsp;

- Serve as a strategic partner in planning future UX architecture and platform expansion.&nbsp;

- Own&nbsp;usability planning, testing,&nbsp;insight development, and documentation.&nbsp;

- &nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;

- Bachelor&rsquo;s degree in&nbsp;graphic design,&nbsp;interaction&nbsp;design,&nbsp;computer&nbsp;science&nbsp;or relevant field&nbsp;from&nbsp;a&nbsp;four-year college or university.&nbsp;
- 5+&nbsp;years of related UX Design experience, preferably in in manufacturing.&nbsp;
- Deep understanding of UX principles, interaction design, and visual systems.&nbsp;
- Expertise in design system architecture and component-driven design.&nbsp;
- Knowledge of responsive, adaptive, and platform-specific design patterns.&nbsp;
- Familiarity with accessibility standards (e.g., WCAG) and inclusive design practices.&nbsp;
- Understanding of front-end technologies and how design translates to code (e.g., design tokens, component libraries).&nbsp;
- Experience&nbsp;designing&nbsp;multiple device ecosystems, including mobile and embedded interfaces.&nbsp;
- Awareness of modern UX research and usability testing methods.
- Exceptional communication and cross-functional collaboration ability.&nbsp;
- Advanced proficiency with design tools (e.g., Figma, adobe products, especially illustrator &amp; photoshop).&nbsp;
- Ability to simplify complex workflows into intuitive systems.&nbsp;
- Strategic thinking paired with hands-on execution.&nbsp;
- Excellent documentation and presentation skills.&nbsp;
- Strong prioritization and decision-making in fast-moving environments.&nbsp;
- Work authorization in the US is required for all candidates.&nbsp;

Job Title: Assitant Designer/Design Coordinator, Apparel
Office Location: Los Angeles, CA&nbsp;
Salary Range: $70,000 - $75,000


ABOUT CUPSHE&nbsp;


Cupshe is a global fashion and lifestyle brand dedicated to creating accessible, trend-forward products that inspire confidence and joy. As the apparel business continues to expand, we are seeking a highly organized, detail-oriented Assistant Designer to support the VP of Apparel Design in building a scalable, customer-focused apparel division.&nbsp;


At Cupshe, we believe technology and AI can enhance creativity, improve communication, and accelerate product development. We encourage curiosity, innovation, and exploration of new tools that help teams work more efficiently and bring ideas to life.&nbsp;


This role is ideal for someone who is passionate about product, enjoys both creative and operational work, and thrives in a fast-paced, entrepreneurial environment. The Assistant Designer will play a critical role in supporting seasonal collections, celebrity and influencer collaborations, B2B development programs, fit initiatives, and fabric development projects.&nbsp;


It is a hybrid schedule, 3 days working in the office is required.


RESPONSIBILITIES&nbsp;


Design &amp; Development&nbsp;
• Support the VP of Apparel Design throughout all phases of the design and development process. 
• Create and revise CAD sketches, technical flats, colorways, and concept presentations using Adobe Illustrator, AI-powered design tools, or a combination of both. 
• Conduct trend, market, and competitive research to support seasonal development. 
• Assist in developing apparel collections across dresses, tops, bottoms, sweaters, outerwear, and special projects. 
• Create presentation boards, concept decks, and seasonal line review materials. 
• Support celebrity, influencer, city, and special collaboration capsules from concept through development. 
• Utilize AI-powered creative tools to support concept development, trend research, color exploration, print ideation, presentation creation, and visual communication. 
• Explore new technologies and workflows that improve design efficiency, communication, and product development.&nbsp;


Product Development Support&nbsp;
• Assist in launching and tracking fabrics, trims, prints, washes, and new developments. 
• Maintain accurate style information, BOMs, line plans, and seasonal design documentation. 
• Partner with Product Development and Supply Chain teams to ensure timely follow-up on design requests and sample status.&nbsp;
• Support development and implementation of Cupshe's core fabric library initiative. 
• Track development calendars and key milestones to support on-time execution across multiple programs.&nbsp;


Fit &amp; Technical Support&nbsp;
• Support fit review process through organization, documentation, and communication of fit comments across U.S. and China teams. 
